    lines=['','### PHASE 6 completion — real export, proof, mainnet mint and native acknowledgment', '',f"Completed {result['observed_at']}. The scheduled daily run completed epoch **{n['finalized_epoch']}**, NAV **{n['nav_per_unit']/1e6:.6f}**, with six-validator verification. The scheduled service exited after a validator-5 read hit storage_writer_busy. Its submit at h1352 and finalize at h1353 were already accepted. After verifying all six receipts and full-ledger equality, Phase 6 acquired the released TEE lock and submitted only the untouched pricing tail; no accepted operation was repeated. The original failure and failed systemd Result are preserved, and the service was not restarted. The small export began only after verified daily completion with MainPID=0. No AWS instance was manually started by this phase; the pre-authorized daily reserved $8.04, cumulative **$48.22 / $100**, remaining **$51.78**. Daily unit configuration and validator runtimes were unchanged; the GPU server version remained 6.3.1. The operational read helper now uses the resident status RPC with its one-second cache bound and bounded read-only retries; literal receipts and full-ledger comparisons remain required.", '', f'The small test used **{paid/1e6:.6f} existing Alice PFUSDC(F)** for a new paid **1-B24** reservation/subscription and actual live export. Every signed transaction first passed the exact live-parent canary and then a literal accepted receipt on all six with full-ledger equality. Authentic finalized public history was captured immediately at the export boundary; the frozen V2 exporter, native verification and guest execution passed. The existing shared GPU produced the real Groth16 receipt proof under its lock. Exact bytes passed a fresh mainnet fork, with malformed-proof, paused-mint, altered-amount and replay negatives. No committee/finality or funding fixture was used for this small live test.', '', '| Mainnet test step | Transaction | Block | Gas |','|---|---|---:|---:|']
